  "scope": "K_r=E_a tensor_i(I+z_i X_a), norm X<=2/3, linear term zero, log converges whenever exp(S)-1-S<1 with S=(2/3)sum |z_i|; scaled z_i=3x/r gives radius above. Conditional expectation onto one Weyl direction before log gives scalar uniform eigenconfiguration F_r=(117+(1+2x/r)^r+2(1-x/r)^r)/120, limit F=(117+exp(2x)+2exp(-x))/120. Its cumulants and nearest zeros are scalar, not full operator spectrum. Applying the dephased two-site weight independently on graph edges yields ferromagnetic 3-state Potts, with Dobrushin influence <=tanh(J/2); at t in [0,3] (positive original factors), max degree12 satisfies contraction 4/9, no spontaneous symmetry breaking in this supplied pair model. Shared global tick alone permutation invariant, cannot distinguish spatial graphs. No physical RG or native dimension selection."
